n":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 60\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>60\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 66\u00b0F, and the record is 87\u00b0F (1973). The low of <strong>42\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Childress is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Childress' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Childress has set <strong>54 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 92 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">152 record highs</strong>, far more than the 92 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (58). Childress' all-time high is 117\u00b0F, on June 27, 1994.","t_chg":"Childress' nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 96 complete years: Childress' average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.24), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1903. Childress' average high shows no clear change: +0.10\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.03 to +0.22) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.64\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.36 to +0.91) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.85\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.48 to +1.23). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 7 of 12 months. Highs rose in none.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Childress' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.03 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 23.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1941 (50.02 in); the driest, 1956 (10.44 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 13 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}